A Caesar cipher: each letter moves three places on, wrapping from z to a and Z to A. Other bytes are copied unchanged.
The probe is string in, string out: the input and the output are both strings, and the output is built one byte at a time with a cell per byte.
---
---
(fn s
	(let shift (fn c
			(if (< c 65) c
					(if (< 90 c)
							(if (< c 97) c
									(if (< 122 c) c (+ 97 (% (+ (- c 97) 3) 26))))
							(+ 65 (% (+ (- c 65) 3) 26)))))
		(letrec go (fn l
				(if (? l) ~ [(shift (head l)) (go (tail l))]))
			(go s))))
---
"" => "" fuel 200000
"abc" => "def" fuel 200000
"Hello, World!" => "Khoor, Zruog!" fuel 200000
"xyz XYZ" => "abc ABC" fuel 200000
"a1 b2 z" => "d1 e2 c" fuel 200000
"~ ok" => "~ rn" fuel 200000
